on a user-selected rectangular region of interest (ROI). The ROI is defined by normalized coordinates (x1,y1) to (x2,y2) in the -1 to 1 range, with frame and state timestamps for synchronization with the video stream.", :interaction {:category :actuator, :ui-pattern :action-button, :feedback :fire-and-forget, :purpose "Focuses camera on user-selected region of interest", :related-state ["proto/proto/proto/proto/proto/ser.JonGuiDataCameraHeat"], :related-commands ["proto/proto/proto/proto/proto/cmd.HeatCamera.TrackROI" "proto/proto/proto/proto/proto/cmd.HeatCamera.ZoomROI"], :notes "User draws rectangle on video to select focus area"}}, "cmd.System.StepMinute" {:id "cmd.System.StepMinute", :name "StepMinute", :package "cmd.System", :source "jon_shared_cmd_system.proto", :fields [{:number 1, :name "offset", :type :int32, :interaction {:semantic-type :count, :unit "minutes", :precision 0}}], :description "Increments or decrements the device's manual time minute value by the specified offset. Positive values increment and negative values decrement the minute. The UI provides buttons for -5, -1, +1, and +5 minute adjustments.", :interaction {:category :settings, :ui-pattern :stepper, :feedback :fire-and-forget, :purpose "Increments or decrements system time by minutes", :related-state ["proto/proto/proto/proto/proto/ser.JonGuiDataSystem"], :related-commands ["proto/proto/proto/proto/proto/cmd.System.SetTimeAndZone" "proto/proto/proto/proto/proto/cmd.System.StepHour"], :preconditions ["Manual time mode must be enabled"]}}, "cmd.DayCamGlassHeater.Stop" {:id "cmd.DayCamGlassHeater.Stop", :name "Stop", :package "cmd.DayCamGlassHeater", :source "jon_shared_cmd_day_cam_glass_heater.proto", :fields [], :description "Stops the day camera glass heater control module and disables its heating timer. This lifecycle command shuts down the heater subsystem entirely, which is different from TurnOff which only deactivates the heating element while keeping the module running.", :interact